| `shell.test_suffixes` | list of strings | `[".bats"]` | a non-empty list, each a `.` and at least one more character, with no whitespace or `/` | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.test_suffixes` row | Sets which file names make a file a shell test, which `make test-sh` runs and the lint and format targets do not judge. Shell scripts with no test file make `make test-sh` exit 13. A malformed list is exit 14. Absent, the targets write `[using default] shell.test_suffixes = [".bats"]` to stderr. | scripts: `shell.script_suffixes` | always |
